   "is_root": true,
   "etymology": "From Proto-Albanian *bá(r)śtᵊkə, with r-loss before a fricative (see buzë) and postsynocopal simplification of the plosive cluster tᵊk > tk > k, from Pre-Proto-Albanian *bárśtukā-, from Proto-Indo-European *bʰórs-tu-kah₂- (“mass of hair”), collective of Proto-Indo-European *bʰorstu-kó- (“hairy”).\nAn origin from Proto-Albanian *baskā, from Proto-Indo-European *bʰask- (“bundle”), is unlikely as the PIE *-sk- cluster would lead to Albanian -h-, not -shk- (*-sk- > *-hk- > *-kh- > *-kʰ- > -h-). The Proto-Albanian form itself would have been *bakʰā > *bahë.",
   "etymology_class": "inherited",
   "source_lang": null,
   "parents": [
    "hairy"
   ],
